(Design Notes:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Even though the ESP32-WROOM-32D is marked as NRND) Tj
T* (\(Not Recommended for New Designs\), it was selected for) Tj
T* (the GCM board due to its large availability in the ) Tj
T* (domestic market and low cost in Brazil;) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The same criteria were used to select the LM2596 buck ) Tj
T* (converter, TJA1050 CANbus transceiver, ACS712/ACS758 ) Tj
T* (hall-effect current sensors, and CH340 USB-TTL bridge. ) Tj
T* (Better options aren't easily available, so the best ) Tj
T* (available choice was selected;) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Other components, such as the ADuM3160 and BSN20,) Tj
T* (were selected for their functionality in the application, ) Tj
T* (making it inevitable to import these ) Tj
T* (components from the international market;) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (-------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T* (In the simulation to the side, it´s possible to see) Tj
T* (the behavior of the pi filter designed to filter the) Tj
T* (supply rail of the ADS1115 analog-to-digital converter;) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The simulation was performed in LTspice software,) Tj
T* (and the simulated components match the real) Tj
T* (specs of the components sold in the market;) Tj
T* (\(see: datasheets/capacitor_filtro_pi\)) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Based on the simulation, it is possible to see that the ) Tj
T* (behavior of the filter is sufficiently efficient to attenuate) Tj
T* (the high frequency ripple generated by the LM2596 at ) Tj
T* (150kHz fixed switching frequency \(-56dB\).) Tj
T* (Thus it is expected that this ripple will not affect the ) Tj
T* (analog section of the circuit;) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The decoupling capacitors are meant to be placed as ) Tj
T* (close as possible to the ICs.) Tj
T* (-------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T* (The four mounting holes are intended to contact the robot's ) Tj
T* (chassis for grounding redundance. Leaving these GND points ) Tj
T* (disconnected is not a issue, as the main connector includes ) Tj
T* (redundant GND lines, unless otherwise specified by ) Tj
T* (the application.) Tj
